.TH "rofi\-rbw" "1" "2026\-09\-06" "Version 1.7.0" "Rofi Third\-party Add\-on Documentation"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBrofi\-rbw\fR \- A rofi frontend for the alternative Bitwarden client \fBrbw\fR
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBrofi\-rbw\fR [\fIOPTION\fR].\&.\&.\&
.PP
\fBrofi\-rbw\fR \fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.PP
\fBrofi\-rbw\fR \fB\-\-version\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBrofi\-rbw\fR is a frontend for the alternative Bitwarden client \fBrbw\fR(1).\&
It presents the entries of your Bitwarden vault in \fBrofi\fR or another
dmenu\-like selector (rofi\-likes), and types, copies, or prints the
components of the selected entry.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-\-action\fR=\fIACTION\fR, \fB\-a\fR \fIACTION\fR
.RS 4
Possible values: \fItype\fR (default), \fIcopy\fR, \fIprint\fR
.PP
Choose what to do with the selected entry: type it using the
"Typer", copy it to the clipboard using the "Clipboarder", or print
it to standard output.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-target\fR=\fITARGET\fR, \fB\-t\fR \fITARGET\fR
.RS 4
Possible values: \fIusername\fR, \fIpassword\fR, \fItotp\fR, \fInotes\fR, \fInumber\fR,
\fIcardholder\fR, \fIbrand\fR, \fIexpiry\fR, \fIcode\fR, \fICUSTOM FIELD NAME\fR,
\fImenu\fR
.PP
Choose which component of the selected entry to type, copy, or
print.\& Can be passed multiple times to use multiple targets.\& Not
all entries have all fields.\& \fImenu\fR is a special value that opens
the target menu.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-prompt\fR=\fIPROMPT\fR, \fB\-r\fR \fIPROMPT\fR
.RS 4
Set the text of the prompt.\& Default is "Choose entry".\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-display\-fields\fR=\fIDISPLAY_FIELDS\fR [\fIDISPLAY_FIELDS\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Possible values: \fIname_only\fR, \fIname_with_folder\fR, \fIfolder\fR,
\fIuser\fR, \fIuri\fR
.PP
Ordered list of fields to show in the selection list, given as
separate arguments (e.\&g.\& \fB\-\-display\-fields\fR \fIname_only\fR \fIuser\fR).\&
\fIname_with_folder\fR renders as \fIfolder/name\fR.\& Defaults to
\fIname_with_folder\fR \fIuser\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-folder\fR (deprecated)
.RS 4
Don'\&t show folders in the list of possible entries.\& Superseded by
\fB\-\-display\-fields\fR; translates to \fB\-\-display\-fields\fR \fIname_only\fR
\fIuser\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-keybindings\fR=\fIKEYBINDINGS\fR
.RS 4
Define custom keybindings in the format
\fI<shortcut>:<action>:<target>\fR, where \fIshortcut\fR is the desired
keybinding, \fIaction\fR is one of the values of \fB\-\-action\fR, and
\fItarget\fR is one of the values of \fB\-\-target\fR.\& Multiple keybindings
are concatenated with a comma; multiple targets for one shortcut
are concatenated with a colon.\& Within a sequence, the special
targets \fIenter\fR, \fItab\fR, and \fIdelay\fR can be used; \fIdelay\fR waits for
the duration given by \fB\-\-action\-sequence\-delay\fR.\&
.PP
This feature is only available in selectors that support custom
keybindings (currently \fBrofi\fR and \fBfuzzel\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-menu\-keybindings\fR=\fIKEYBINDINGS\fR
.RS 4
Define custom keybindings for the target menu in the format
\fI<shortcut>:<action>\fR.\& Multiple keybindings are concatenated with
a comma.\&
.PP
This feature is only available in selectors that support custom
keybindings.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-clear\-after\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
.RS 4
Clear the password from the clipboard after \fISECONDS\fR seconds.\& Set
to 0 (the default) to disable.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-action\-sequence\-delay\fR=\fIMILLISECONDS\fR
.RS 4
Define the duration to wait for a \fIdelay\fR step in a keybinding
sequence (e.\&g.\& \fIAlt+c:copy:username:delay:password\fR).\& It applies
to both \fItype\fR and \fIcopy\fR actions.\& 1000 by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-typing\-start\-delay\fR=\fIMILLISECONDS\fR
.RS 4
Set a delay before typing starts.\& 0 by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-typing\-key\-delay\fR=\fIMILLISECONDS\fR
.RS 4
Set a delay between key presses when typing.\& 0 by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-selector\fR=\fISELECTOR\fR
.RS 4
Possible values: \fIrofi\fR, \fIwofi\fR, \fIfuzzel\fR, \fIbemenu\fR
.PP
Choose the selector application manually.\& Usually \fIrofi\fR, but on
Wayland you may want \fIwofi\fR.\& Chosen automatically by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-selector\-args\fR=\fISELECTOR_ARGS\fR
.RS 4
A string of arguments to give to the selector.\& Due to an argparse
limitation, specify it as \fB\-\-selector\-args\fR=\fIARGS\fR or
\fB\-\-selector\-args\fR " ARGS".\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-clipboarder\fR=\fICLIPBOARDER\fR
.RS 4
Possible values: \fIxsel\fR, \fIxclip\fR, \fIwl\-copy\fR
.PP
Choose the application to access the clipboard with manually.\&
Chosen automatically by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-typer\fR=\fITYPER\fR
.RS 4
Possible values: \fIxdotool\fR, \fIwtype\fR, \fIydotool\fR, \fIdotool\fR
.PP
Choose the application to type with manually.\& Chosen
automatically by default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-use\-notify\-send\fR
.RS 4
Send a desktop notification after each field is copied (e.\&g.\&
"username copied to clipboard").\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
.RS 4
Disable the automatic frecency cache.\& It contains sha1\-hashes of
the selected entries and how often they were used.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-help\fR
.RS 4
Don'\&t show the help message about the available keyboard shortcuts.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print brief usage information and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print the version number and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.PP
The following keybindings are active by default (configurable via
\fB\-\-keybindings\fR):
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fIEnter\fR: perform the default action (see \fB\-\-action\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+1\fR: type the username and the password, separated with a \fItab\fR
character
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+2\fR: type the username
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+3\fR: type the password
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+4\fR: type the TOTP
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+c\fR: copy the password
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+u\fR: copy the username
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+t\fR: copy the TOTP
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+m\fR: show a menu of the entry'\&s components
.IP \(bu 4
\fIAlt+s\fR: sync the contents of the vault
.PD
.PP
The autotyping sequence of \fIAlt+1\fR can also be defined as a custom
field named \fIautotype\fR on each credential.\&
.PP
Custom keybindings are only supported by the \fIrofi\fR and \fIfuzzel\fR
selectors; \fIwofi\fR and \fIbemenu\fR only provide the default \fIEnter\fR
confirmation.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Options starting with \fB\-\-\fR can also be set in a config file.\& The
config file syntax allows: \fIkey = value\fR for options taking a value,
\fIflag = true\fR for boolean options, and \fIstuff = [a, b, c]\fR for
list\-valued options.\& If an option is specified in more than one place,
command\-line values override values from the config file.\&
.PP
The config file is searched for at \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rofi\-rbw.\&rc\fR and
in the directories listed in \fI$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR.\&
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fI\(ti/.\&config/rofi\-rbw.\&rc\fR
.RS 4
Per\-user configuration file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI/etc/xdg/rofi\-rbw.\&rc\fR
.RS 4
System\-wide configuration file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fI\(ti/.\&cache/rofi\-rbw.\&runcache\fR
.RS 4
Saves the number of times an entry has been used, so that
frequently used entries can be sorted first.\& Entries are hashed
with sha1 so as not to leak any secrets.\&
.PP
.RE
